Subject: [PATCH] volume: compare cluster, not host, on in-place retype

VolumeRetypeWithoutMigrationTest.test_available_volume_retype retypes a
volume with migration_policy='never' and asserts that
os-vol-host-attr:host is unchanged. That only holds when cinder-volume
is not clustered. With Active/Active (cinder-volume `cluster =` set) the
scheduler matches the volume's cluster in find_retype_backend(), and
VolumeManager.retype() writes the selected backend's host and
cluster_name back to the volume. That host can be any member of the
cluster, so the host attribute moves while the volume stays on the same
backend:

    testtools.matchers._impl.MismatchError: !=:
    reference = 'testbed-node-0@rbd-volumes#volumes'
    actual    = 'testbed-node-2@rbd-volumes#volumes'

The failure is random: it fires only when the request lands on a
scheduler whose cluster entry carries a different member than the one
that created the volume.

Compare cluster_name instead when the volume is clustered, and keep the
host comparison otherwise. cluster_name is always compared, so a volume
that gains or loses a cluster still fails. Cinder returns cluster_name
in the admin volume details only from microversion 3.61 (and then as
null when not clustered), so the class now requests 3.61. It is skipped
where [volume] max_microversion is below 3.61 or unset.

This follows the approach of the abandoned upstream change
https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/tempest/+/708332 (which cannot
be used as is) for https://bugs.launchpad.net/tempest/+bug/1863729, still
open; tempest master still asserts the host. Drop this patch once
requirements.txt moves to a tempest release that fixes that bug; the
Containerfile's dry-run will fail the build and force exactly that.

--- a/tempest/api/volume/admin/test_volume_retype.py
+++ b/tempest/api/volume/admin/test_volume_retype.py
@@ -166,6 +166,10 @@
 class VolumeRetypeWithoutMigrationTest(VolumeRetypeTest):
     """Test volume retype without migration"""
 
+    # 3.61 adds cluster_name to the admin volume details.
+    volume_min_microversion = '3.61'
+    volume_max_microversion = 'latest'
+
     @classmethod
     def resource_setup(cls):
         super(VolumeRetypeWithoutMigrationTest, cls).resource_setup()
@@ -176,9 +180,15 @@
 
         keys_with_no_change = ('id', 'size', 'description', 'name',
                                'user_id', 'os-vol-tenant-attr:tenant_id',
-                               'os-vol-host-attr:host')
+                               'cluster_name')
         keys_with_change = ('volume_type',)
 
+        # In an Active/Active cluster any member may perform the retype and
+        # record itself as the volume's host, so only the cluster must stay
+        # the same there.
+        if not volume_source['cluster_name']:
+            keys_with_no_change += ('os-vol-host-attr:host',)
+
         # Check the volume information after the retype
         self.assertIsNone(volume_dest['os-vol-mig-status-attr:migstat'])
         self.assertIsNone(volume_dest['migration_status'])
@@ -198,7 +208,8 @@
         1. Create volume1 with volume_type1
         2. Retype volume1 to volume_type2 with migration_policy='never'
         3. Check volume1's volume_type is changed to volume_type2, and
-           'os-vol-host-attr:host' in the volume info is not changed.
+           its cluster_name is not changed; for a volume that is not in a
+           cluster, 'os-vol-host-attr:host' is not changed either.
         """
         src_vol = self.create_volume(volume_type=self.src_vol_type['name'])
 
